As you turn the steering wheel, your van wants to keep moving in a straight line, but the friction of your tires "pulls" you toward the center of the turn. This inward pull keeps you on a curved path instead of flying off the road in a straight line. 

In orbit, gravity acts like those tires. The satellite has a high forward speed, and gravity constantly "tugs" it toward the Earth. Because the satellite is moving fast enough, this tug isn't strong enough to crash it into the ground; instead, it just curves the satellite's path into a circle around the planet. 

With that in mind, take another look at the options in your quiz. Which one best describes that balance between moving forward and being pulled toward the center?"
